			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Enforce context-menu visibility and titlebar spacing\n\nExtend the `Apply/Pipeline` orchestration to activate `InjectMacTitlebarOffsetCSS` and `InjectPartZIndexCSS` plugins, resolving layer conflicts in the Tauri WKWebView context.\n\nThe `InjectPartZIndexCSS` plugin overrides VS Code's implicit stacking order by pinning `.context-view` (menubar dropdowns, command palette, right-click menus) to `z-index: 2600`, ensuring they render above the editor content and titlebar. It also explicitly handles `.context-view.fixed` and `.shadow-root-host` to counteract `all: initial` resets and Shadow DOM isolation issues. Additionally, `.monaco-hover` and `.editor-widget` are pinned to `z-index: 50` to maintain visibility for inline suggestions.\n\nSimultaneously, `InjectMacTitlebarOffsetCSS` reserves the width of the macOS traffic-light controls on the titlebar's left edge, preventing the in-window menubar and command-center quick-pick from colliding with the OS-painted window controls.\n\nThese changes eliminate menu visibility bugs and ensure the native window controls do not overlap the application interface.",
			"SHA": "0cc859c27f7c609872bfb9e846c10a25179ea30c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T22:38:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				725,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Establish deterministic z-index hierarchy and restore macOS titlebar spacing\n\nExtend the `Apply/Pipeline` orchestration to include `InjectPartZIndexCSS` and `InjectMacTitlebarOffset` plugins, addressing rendering layer conflicts in the Tauri webview context.\n\nThe z-index patch (`Plugin/Polyfill/Part/Z/Index/CSS.ts`) overrides VS Code's default stacking to ensure floating UI elements render correctly. It explicitly pins `.context-view` (dropdowns, command palette, right-click menus) at `z-index: 2600`, ensuring they appear above the editor content and the titlebar, preventing the menubar dropdowns from rendering behind the editor pane due to isolation conflicts. It also pins `.monaco-hover` and `.editor-widget` at `z-index: 50` to maintain visibility for inline suggestions.\n\nSimultaneously, update `README.md` with a standardized directory tree reflecting the expanded plugin structure and new configuration profiles.\n\nThese changes resolve menu visibility issues and ensure the macOS traffic-light controls do not overlap the in-window menubar.",
			"SHA": "84a65d05c1a12086b9b8d08da75b22c2185a1185"
		},
