				725,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Standardize inline code formatting for Rest and esbuild\n\nUpdate the `README.md` to consistently wrap the `Rest` compiler and `esbuild` tool names in backticks within the 'Artifact Merging' feature description. This aligns the documentation with the project's strict PascalCase and formatting standards for technical identifiers.\n\nNo functional changes to the build pipeline are introduced.",
			"SHA": "95060185cd4e4a9eb1e05177df82a5a3f7b8d613"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:54:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				725,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Standardize inline code formatting in README\n\nUpdate the `README.md` to consistently wrap all technical identifiers, compiler names, and pipeline components (e.g., `VSCode`, `Rest`, `OXC`, `esbuild`, `Sky`, `Wind`, `Cocoon`) in backticks. This aligns the documentation with the project's strict PascalCase and formatting standards.\n\nAdditionally, regenerate the source map artifact for the `Patch/Webview/Iframe/Service/Worker` transform to reflect the latest build configuration state.",
			"SHA": "a2ba887b1c585a640e584a049cef1c3eb129492a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:13:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				725,
				113
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Standardize code formatting and extend WebKit DOMContentLoaded patches\n\nReformat the entire Output build configuration tree to conform to the project's strict PascalCase and indentation standards. This affects esbuild configuration files (`ESBuild/`), the main pipeline orchestrator (`Apply/Pipeline.js`), service copiers (`Plugin/Copy/`), and the comprehensive suite of transform plugins (`Plugin/Transform/` and `Plugin/Polyfill/`). The diff reflects a comprehensive whitespace normalization pass across hundreds of files.\n\nAdditionally, extend the `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` transform to address a critical WebKit rendering deadlock in Tauri's WKWebView context. The previous fix removed the `allowScripts` guard for Safari, but the subsequent `DOMContentLoaded` polling logic still erroneously gated on `contentDocument.location.pathname.endsWith('/fake.html')`. Due to WebKit bug #238901, `location.pathname` is often empty or undefined in custom-protocol contexts during the polling phase, causing the condition to fail and the editor to hang on the `fake.html` placeholder.\n\nThis patch removes the pathname dependency, enforcing a `readyState !== 'loading'` check for all Safari/WebKit runtimes. This ensures the polling fallback activates reliably regardless of the URL state, unblocking the webview bootstrap.\n\nThe build output artifacts in `Configuration` and `Source` are regenerated to reflect these source transformations and formatting updates.",
			"SHA": "5b81af93f224a85e83cffcfb21fa0a8647297f91"
		}
	],
